				<r3d:description language="eng">&lt;&lt;&lt;!!!&lt;&lt;&lt; 2019-12-23: the repository is offline &gt;&gt;&gt;!!!&gt;&gt;&gt; Introduction of genome-scale metabolic network:
The completion of genome sequencing and subsequent functional annotation for a great number of species enables the reconstruction of genome-scale metabolic networks. These networks, together with in silico network analysis methods such as the constraint based methods (CBM) and graph theory methods, can provide us systems level understanding of cellular metabolism. Further more, they can be applied to many predictions of real biological application such as: gene essentiality analysis, drug target discovery and metabolic engineering</r3d:description>
